  "id": "1ad10300-ae57-45df-aced-ed6f616b5542",
  "title": "T2LSC-Bench: Benchmarking Localized Semantic Control in Text-to-Image Generation",
  "summary": "T2LSC-Bench introduces a controlled diagnostic benchmark to evaluate localized semantic control in text-to-image generation, addressing issues like target-text-associated semantic leakage. It provides a framework for measuring Text-at-Anchor Accuracy (TAA), Semantic Subject Preservation (SSP), and Conditional Semantic Leakage Rate (cSLR) through a dual-branch protocol. This benchmark helps identify challenges in rendering text within designated regions without altering identity or semantics.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "T2LSC-Bench introduces a controlled diagnostic benchmark to evaluate localized semantic control in text-to-image generation, addressing issues like target-text-associated semantic leakage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It includes 50 seed subjects and 1,200 prompt cases per model, resulting in 7,160 evaluated images across six models.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The dual-branch protocol combines OCR-VLM text verification with structured VLM semantic judgments to measure TAA, SSP, and cSLR.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
